A||||3||griffin||Going to look @ an 85 GT any tips?||||1||
Z||000000||griffin||06-25-2001||01:08 AM||||Tomaorrow I am going to look at an 85 GT with a/c pw,pl,pm sunroof auto. Any tips that I should look for or know before purchasing? Any help would be appreciated. <BR>Griffin||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroKyle||06-25-2001||01:15 AM||||be careful, lol, =). Damaged rocker panels, quarter windows are common.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg"> <BR>My Fast 'n Black Car<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||06-25-2001||03:03 PM||||check: for oil leaks (espec. dist. O-ring and<BR>rear valve cover, exhaust leak on manifolds,<BR>rust on frame and inside shock towers in originally from salty state, make sure the front (by front I mean closest to pass. compartment) spark plugs have been or can be<BR>changed. Some people don't change the Fiero's<BR>spark plugs on that side because of difficulty and then they become a permanent part of the head!<BR>Also: check oil for antifreeze and trans oil<BR>if auto. Everything else should show itself on the test drive. keep in mind the age of this car. It won't be perfect.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||BC-GT||06-25-2001||03:56 PM||||Don't know if you have safeties out there but if you do and need the e-brake, check it carefully, can run into big bucks and headaches. I had to replace rear calipers, cables and the handle itself.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
